+
+---
+
+## Visit
+
+**Dybbøl Banke**, Sundeved. The redoubt line is marked on the ground and the mill
+has been rebuilt again. The view south to Broager church explains the battle better
+than any account of it: the towers the Prussian gunners spotted from are still
+there, and still in range.
+
+**Sankelmark**, south of Flensburg. A memorial by the road where the rearguard
+turned on 6 February 1864.
+
+**Flensborg Gamle Kirkegård.** Chapter 33 closes here. The Isted Lion, taken to
+Berlin in 1864 and to Copenhagen in 1945, came back in 2011.
+
+**Als Sund** at Sottrupskov. The Prussians crossed here in rowing boats before dawn
+on 29 June 1864. It is a short row.
+
+**Bæksgårde**, Give parish, and the memorial stone north of Kolding. Wreaths are
+still laid at the stone for Niels Kjeldsen on 1 March, or on 29 February in a leap
+year.
+
+**Brumleby**, Østerbro, Copenhagen. Lægeforeningens Boliger, built after the
+cholera of 1853, where Ilia Fibiger raised her foster daughters and wore herself
+out.
+
+**Kongeåen.** The stream was a state frontier from 1864 to 1920, and the old
+customs houses are still standing along it.
